# Product shell

The tax-docs client is a **clone of Ramp's product app** (`try.ramp.com`), relabeled for CPA document work. Tokens: `.cursor/rules/design-system.mdc`. Interaction/voice: `.cursor/rules/web-ui.mdc`. How the pieces compose: `.cursor/skills/building-product-ui/SKILL.md`.

One layout tree. Shell markup and shared helpers live in `src/client/app/render.ts`; chrome CSS in `src/client/styles/shell.css`. Do not add a second shell, a React tree, or a page that skips the recipes below.

## Page framework

`src/client/main.ts` runs one loop: `parseRoute(pathname)` → `moduleFor(route)` → `load()` (skeleton on screen) → `render()` into `.workspace` → `bind()` → `startPolling` when the module sets `pollMs`. Poll updates replace the `.workspace` node so delegated listeners die with the old node; unchanged HTML skips bind. `dialogOpen(workspace)` skips replace (and re-bind) while `[data-new-engagement-modal]:not([hidden])`, `.side-panel`, or `[data-export-confirm-modal]:not([hidden])` is present so focus and keystrokes survive the tick. Polling stops on navigation, and a stale load never paints over a newer one.

- Routes: `src/client/app/router.ts` returns a `Route` union. Path params only — `?tab=`, `?new=1` are view state a page reads from `window.location.search`.
- Pages: `src/client/app/pages/*.ts` each export a `PageModule<T>` (`load` / `render` / optional `bind` / optional `pollMs`) registered in `pages/registry.ts`. `moduleFor` is exhaustive: every route resolves, so navigation can never throw.
- Data: `src/client/app/api.ts` (`getJson`, `sendJson`, `uploadFile`, `startPolling`) is the only fetch seam. Responses parse through `src/shared/schemas/api.ts` — the same schemas the server builds its payloads with.
- Failures: `ApiError.message` is the server's own `{ error }` string and pages render it verbatim next to a retry control. A generic "something went wrong" is a regression.
- The `portal` route renders chromeless (`.app-chromeless`) — no sidebar, no palette, no nav links.

No fixture module. If a page needs data, it fetches it.

## Chrome

`.app` is `256px` bone sidebar + white workspace. The sidebar is sticky (`position: sticky; top: 0; height: 100vh; overflow-y: auto`) so only the workspace scrolls; the 960px stacked layout overrides it back to static. Optional `298px` right rail on Home only. Settings live in `.sidebar-foot`. Search is `Ctrl+K` → Command K (bone 80% wash, 640×432 white panel, grouped list, Feather search on the right). `.palette[hidden]` must stay `display: none`. Collapse is `.app.is-collapsed` at `--app-sidebar-collapsed-width` (60px). Collapsed header is one slot: the GB mark grows to `--icon-size-brand-collapsed` (28px) and is centered (`justify-content: center` on `.sidebar-head` — the expanded `space-between` must not leak through). The expand control sits absolutely on top of it at `opacity: 0` until `.sidebar-head:hover` or `:focus-within`. Do not stack logo and toggle as two visible rows, and do not leave the expand button `space-between` next to the logo in that rail. Collapsed nav/search/expand icons use `--icon-size-nav-collapsed` 16px; expanded stays `--icon-size-nav` 12px. Expanded brand stays `--icon-size-brand` 20px.

Idle nav is ash on bone. An expanded group is a `4px` hairline wash (`--surface-nav-active`) wrapping parent + children. The current child punches out as a bone chip — matched by comparing the child `href` to `pathname + search`, so `?tab=needs-review` moves the punch-out. An unmatched child href (for example `/documents?tab=trusted`) leaves the parent group active and marks no `is-current` child — do not fall back to index 0. Nested rows keep a `12px` `.nav-icon-spacer` so labels line up. Children render only while the group is current. Icons are Feather at `--icon-size-nav` 12px expanded (`src/client/app/icons.ts`) — never hand-drawn SVGs. The sidebar brand next to “Tax Docs” is `design-system/gb-favicon.png`, same file as the tab favicon — not a clip-path square.

Nav is Inbox, Home, Documents (children All / Needs review), Engagements, Clients, with Settings in the footer. Engagement detail and export keep the Engagements group current (`navIdForRoute`); review (`/documents/:documentId`) keeps Documents current. Exactly two badges, both live and hidden at zero: the Inbox pill (`/api/inbox/unread-count` — unread THREADS — into `[data-inbox-badge]`) and the Documents pill (`needsReviewCount` from `/api/metrics` into `[data-documents-badge]`, the same count as the Needs review tab). Badge counts must match what their tabs show; no other tab gets a badge.

## Page recipes

| Recipe | Use for | Stack |
|--------|---------|-------|
| **Home** | `/` | Eyebrow greeting, 28px queue title, wash card, `.row-list`, rail of block CTAs + hairline widgets |
| **List** | `/documents`, `/engagements`, `/clients` | `pageHeader` (title + ash count + optional secondary + one real primary; no kebab) → underline `.tabs` (when the page has tabs) → `.filter-bar` (compose `filterSelect` / `filterBar` / `bindFilterBar` from `src/client/app/components/filter-bar.ts`: labeled native selects bound to real data, synced to the URL query string, refetching server-side Mongo filters on change, with a quiet "Clear filters" text link while a filter is active) → `.data-table` with dual-line `.entity` cells. Bind `[data-href]` rows with `bindRowLinks`. Every filter control must be a bound select — no unbound Add-filter pills, no download, and no free-text search until a bound search exists |
| **Inbox** | `/inbox` | `pageHeader` (unread-thread count) + `.inbox-threads` disclosure sections — one thread per engagement's outbound request; request-item status lines (never per-file rows) with `/documents/:id` deep links; shared portal-link control in the thread head; expanding an unread thread marks it read |
| **Settings** | `/settings` | `pageHeader` → tabs → `.definition-grid` (dt ash / dd ink) inside `.settings-block` |
| **Review** | `/documents/:documentId` | `breadcrumbs` (Documents / filename) → `pageHeader` (filename + type name + secondary "Engagement workspace" link) → `.review-split`: sticky hairline `.review-viewer` iframe on the left, `.review-panel` on the right (panel head, compact inline `.review-field` rows, document-scoped validation `.row-list` with passes visible, `.review-foot` single primary) |
| **Portal** | `/portal/:token` (chromeless) | Left request checklist with 16px status marks and collapsible nested files per item, client waive-with-note on open items, one common `.dropzone`, live upload-status list polling every 2s; pipeline stages via the `.chip` recipe with client-facing labels |

A new route picks one recipe. Extend `pageHeader` / `breadcrumbs` / `tabs` / `dataTable` / `bindRowLinks` / `entityCell` / `listRow` / `railWidget` / `pipelineChip` / `stageChip` / `confidenceChip` / `emptyState` — do not fork a lookalike.

Detail pages get `breadcrumbs(items)` from `render.ts` above their `pageHeader`: ash `data-nav-link` anchors with `" / "` separators, last item ink `.breadcrumb-current` (never a link). The engagement workspace leads with `Engagements / {client}`.

## Primitives

Buttons live in `design-system/css/base.css`: primary highlighter `0` radius `40px` (hover inverts to ink), secondary `1px --color-outline`, ghost, `32px` `.icon-btn`. Status is `--color-success` / `--color-warning` / `--color-ash` — never highlighter. Elevation is `1px --color-hairline`, not shadow.

The review split is furniture, not a fifth surface: `.review-split` is a two-column grid and `.review-viewer` is a sticky `16px`-radius hairline frame around the stored-PDF iframe. Each `.review-field` is ONE compact hairline-ruled row (~40px): label + `10px` ash `.review-field-type` caption (a caption, never an uppercased UI sentence), an always-editable typed `.review-field-input` pre-filled with `editedValue ?? value` (save-on-change PATCH `{ action: "edit" }`; quiet Saving…/Saved/error hint in `.review-field-state`), and the confidence chip. Per-field accept does not exist — trust auto-finalizes unreviewed fields as accepted. Source snippets live behind a per-row `.review-source-toggle` disclosure, default-collapsed. `.review-foot` holds the single primary; disabled it drops to `--surface-nav-active` + ash so an unavailable action never reads as a live highlighter CTA.

Pipeline state renders through `pipelineChip(status)`: `received` / `quality-review` / `classifying` / `extracting` are ash `.chip-processing`; `needs-review` / `unclassified` are `.chip-warning`; `trusted` is `.chip-success`; `rejected` / `failed` are `.chip-halted` (hairline fill, warning text). Engagement stages render through `stageChip(status)` and extraction confidence through `confidenceChip(value)` — both compose the one `.chip` base (`confidence-high` / `-medium` / `-low` are tier modifiers of it, not a separate component). Chip labels are sentence case, never uppercase. Shared furniture in `shell.css`: `.modal`, `.side-panel`, `.dropzone` (hide native file inputs with `.visually-hidden-input`, never `display: none`), `.page-skeleton`, `.load-error`, `.breadcrumbs`, `.engagement-status` (the one-line workspace status strip: hairline rules, ash labels, ink values — not a metrics ticker), and `.segmented` / `.segmented-option` (the modal two-option choice recipe: visually-hidden real radios in styled labels, selected = ink border on wash; never chips, never highlighter). Chips never stretch in list rows: `.list-row > .chip { justify-self: end }` is a guarantee, not a suggestion. (The former `.ticker` metrics band was removed from Home by operator ruling — do not reintroduce it.)

## Anti-patterns

A second sidebar. Marketing-site tokens (ink `#0c0a08`, `6px` buttons, bone canvas). Nav children without the group wash. Current child that stays hairline instead of punching out to bone. Punching out the first child when no href matches. Lucide/Heroicons/inline path glyphs. Two primary CTAs. Unbound kebab / Add filter / download on list chrome. Drop shadows except `--shadow-palette` on Command K. `font-weight: 600`. A page that invents its own header/table instead of the helpers in `render.ts`. Hardcoded counts, statuses, or fixture rows in markup. A page module that fetches outside `api.ts` or swallows an `ApiError` message. Highlighter on a status chip.
